# Gradle incremental annotation processing registration.
#
# Every processor that generates is registered as AGGREGATING. The mapping family (MappingProcessor,
# MergeProcessor, AssemblyProcessor) genuinely aggregates: MappingProcessor and MergeProcessor
# resolve nesting and sealed dispatch against a registry of the other annotated specs in the
# compilation, so their outputs may depend on any annotated element in it. They also read the
# classpath index (org.higherkindedj.mapping.index) written by dependencies compiled with the
# processor, which no source in the compilation references; Gradle recompiles the source set on a
# classpath change, but a dependency gaining a spec that nothing downstream refers to may need a
# clean downstream build to be seen. The per-type optics generators are likely ISOLATING-safe (one
# annotated type, one origin per generated file), but an ISOLATING claim that turns out wrong
# produces silently stale outputs, while AGGREGATING is behaviour-preserving for every processor.
# Refining individual processors to ISOLATING needs a per-processor one-origin-per-file audit first.
#
# AGGREGATING binds each processor to what a class file carries. In an incremental build Gradle
# hands every unchanged annotated type of the compilation to it by name, and javac reads that type,
# and every unchanged type it names, from the class files the last build wrote, so:
# - each annotation a processor claims is CLASS-retained, or Gradle recompiles the whole source set
#   on every change, and so is each hkj annotation it reads beside one (ProcessorRegistrationTest
#   holds both to that);
# - a parameter name survives only under -parameters, so a generator writing one where it reaches
#   run time refuses a class file without them (MergeProcessor's null checks);
# - no @SuppressWarnings survives, so a suppressible warning about a declaration read from a class
#   file is not reported again (Diagnostics.mayWarn);
# - another library's source-only annotations do not survive either, so a check that reads them,
#   such as the one Lombok's @Singular asks for, is made only where the type is compiled from
#   source, as for a dependency's;
# - javac's Filer writes over a class file it refuses to write over in source, so a generator
#   refuses a name a class file without HKJ's @Generated already has: the mapping, merge, error
#   envelope and iso generators through GeneratedNames, and PathSourceProcessor in its own name
#   checks. The other generators do not refuse one yet.
#
# CompanionAnnotationProcessor only claims the annotations the others read or write. It generates
# nothing, so the one-origin-per-file rule holds for it trivially. ISOLATING leaves Gradle nothing to
# track, where AGGREGATING would reprocess every type carrying them, every generated class included.
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.AccumulatorProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.AssemblyProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.CompanionAnnotationProcessor,isolating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.ErrorEnvelopeProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.FocusProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.FoldProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.ForComprehensionProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.GetterProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.ImportOpticsProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.IsoProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.LensProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.MappingProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.MergeProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.PrismProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.SetterProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.TraversalProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.effect.ComposeEffectsProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.effect.EffectAlgebraProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.effect.PathProcessor,aggregating
org.higherkindedj.optics.processing.effect.PathSourceProcessor,aggregating
